# The Moves page (More controls' first row, 0.1.14) and More controls: the way to VR Options as bodypage.sim goes, by the sticks with
# the right controller off, eleven rows down to VR Controls; there eleven down to its last row, More controls, and A opens it. Its
# first row is a button, Moves: A opens that page. Each row stepped: Swingshot anywhere On, Wall run and jump On, Swingshot reach twice
# (No limit), Wrench throw distance Far, Wrench comes back When you call it. B back to More controls. Two down (past Ledge shimmy),
# Hide black bars stepped right then left: "[vr-view] Hide black bars: off, the game's own", then "on". Two down (past Menu pointer),
# Arm moves stepped: Buttons ("[vr-controls] Arm moves: Buttons"); five down, the page's last, Sparkles on the bolts
# stepped: Off. B back to VR Controls. The [vr-swing] line says "Swingshot anywhere: on", the [vr-rig] lines arm moves
# buttons, then sparkles_in_world off, and no line says a page has more rows than the port's 12; the run's
# vr-options.txt keeps swing_anywhere 1, wall_moves 1, swing_reach 2, wrench_far 1, wrench_stay 1, hide_bars 1 and button_moves 1. (0.1.12's
# VR Controls had 16 rows, and the port shows 12 of a page: its last four could not be reached.)
